{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Dm7qNeJTqHnPGZLWQAMNjd","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tid: srd047-hostname\n2\ttitle: \"cmd/hostname: Print System Hostname\"\n3\t\n4\tproblem: |\n5\t  Scripts and configuration tools use hostname to query the system's network node name.\n6\t  The GNU coreutils hostname is deliberately minimal compared to the net-tools hostname:\n7\t  it prints the hostname and exits. The Go implementation must match the Homebrew GNU\n8\t  reference binary (ghostname, installed by coreutils) byte-for-byte on stdout and exit\n9\t  code, verified by differential testing via pkg/testutils.\n10\t\n11\tgoals:\n12\t  - G1: Print the system hostname followed by a newline.\n13\t  - G2: Reject any extra operands or unsupported flags with an error message and nonzero exit.\n14\t\n15\trequirements:\n16\t  R1:\n17\t    title: Default behavior\n18\t    items:\n19\t      - R1.1:\n20\t          text: When invoked with no arguments, must print the system hostname followed by a newline and exit 0.\n21\t      - R1.2:\n22\t          text: The output must be identical to the value returned by the gethostname(2) syscall on the current system.\n23\t\n24\t  R2:\n25\t    title: Error handling\n26\t    items:\n27\t      - R2.1:\n28\t          text: If any extra operand is provided (beyond --help and --version), must print an error message to stderr and exit 1.\n29\t      - R2.2:\n30\t          text: Must not accept any flags other than --help and --version. Unknown flags must produce an error message to stderr and exit 1.\n31\t\n32\t  R3:\n33\t    title: Differential testing\n34\t    items:\n35\t      - R3.1:\n36\t          text: Differential tests must compare stdout output and exit codes between the Go binary and the reference binary (ghostname) via pkg/testutils.\n37\t      - R3.2:\n38\t          text: \"Tests must cover: normal invocation (no arguments), extra operand error, and unknown flag error.\"\n39\t      - R3.3:\n40\t          text: All differential tests must set LC_ALL=C in the environment.\n41\t\n42\tnon_goals:\n43\t  - cmd/hostname does not set the hostname; it is read-only.\n44\t  - cmd/hostname does not support -s (short), -f (FQDN), -d (domain), or -i (IP) flags found in the net-tools hostname. The GNU coreutils hostname is a simpler utility.\n45\t\n46\tacceptance_criteria:\n47\t  - id: AC1\n48\t    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/hostname prints the system hostname, matching ghostname.\"\n49\t    traces:\n50\t      - R1.1\n51\t      - R1.2\n52\t  - id: AC2\n53\t    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/hostname extraarg exits 1 with an error message to stderr, matching ghostname.\"\n54\t    traces:\n55\t      - R1.1\n56\t      - R2.1\n57\t      - R2.2\n58\t      - R3.1\n59\t      - R3.2\n60\t  - id: AC3\n61\t    criterion: \"Differential test against ghostname passes for normal invocation and error cases.\"\n62\t    traces:\n63\t      - R2.1\n64\t      - R2.2\n65\t      - R3.1\n66\t      - R3.2\n67\t      - R3.3\n68\t  - id: AC4\n69\t    criterion: \"cmd/hostname compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n70\t    traces:\n71\t      - R1.1\n72\t      - R1.2\n73\t      - R2.1\n74\t      - R2.2\n75\t      - R3.1\n76\t      - R3.2\n77\t      - R3.3\n78\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e074febc-29ca-4ae0-8d17-a11ea6e11daa","uuid":"7f7c7cf4-5d2c-4246-854f-8b9a57d2b804","timestamp":"2026-05-14T17:00:57.905Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5187/docs/specs/software-requirements/srd047-hostname.yaml","content":"id: srd047-hostname\ntitle: \"cmd/hostname: Print System Hostname\"\n\nproblem: |\n  Scripts and configuration tools use hostname to query the system's network node name.\n  The GNU coreutils hostname is deliberately minimal compared to the net-tools hostname:\n  it prints the hostname and exits. The Go implementation must match the Homebrew GNU\n  reference binary (ghostname, installed by coreutils) byte-for-byte on stdout and exit\n  code, verified by differential testing via pkg/testutils.\n\ngoals:\n  - G1: Print the system hostname followed by a newline.\n  - G2: Reject any extra operands or unsupported flags with an error message and nonzero exit.\n\nrequirements:\n  R1:\n    title: Default behavior\n    items:\n      - R1.1:\n          text: When invoked with no arguments, must print the system hostname followed by a newline and exit 0.\n      - R1.2:\n          text: The output must be identical to the value returned by the gethostname(2) syscall on the current system.\n\n  R2:\n    title: Error handling\n    items:\n      - R2.1:\n          text: If any extra operand is provided (beyond --help and --version), must print an error message to stderr and exit 1.\n      - R2.2:\n          text: Must not accept any flags other than --help and --version. Unknown flags must produce an error message to stderr and exit 1.\n\n  R3:\n    title: Differential testing\n    items:\n      - R3.1:\n          text: Differential tests must compare stdout output and exit codes between the Go binary and the reference binary (ghostname) via pkg/testutils.\n      - R3.2:\n          text: \"Tests must cover: normal invocation (no arguments), extra operand error, and unknown flag error.\"\n      - R3.3:\n          text: All differential tests must set LC_ALL=C in the environment.\n\nnon_goals:\n  - cmd/hostname does not set the hostname; it is read-only.\n  - cmd/hostname does not support -s (short), -f (FQDN), -d (domain), or -i (IP) flags found in the net-tools hostname. The GNU coreutils hostname is a simpler utility.\n\nacceptance_criteria:\n  - id: AC1\n    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/hostname prints the system hostname, matching ghostname.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.2\n  - id: AC2\n    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/hostname extraarg exits 1 with an error message to stderr, matching ghostname.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R2.1\n      - R2.2\n      - R3.1\n      - R3.2\n  - id: AC3\n    criterion: \"Differential test against ghostname passes for normal invocation and error cases.\"\n    traces:\n      - R2.1\n      - R2.2\n      - R3.1\n      - R3.2\n      - R3.3\n  - id: AC4\n    criterion: \"cmd/hostname compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.2\n      - R2.1\n      - R2.2\n      - R3.1\n      - R3.2\n      - R3.3\n","numLines":78,"startLine":1,"totalLines":78}}}
