{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user (an automated orchestrator) has assigned task #5187: implement `cmd/hostname/main.go` for the go-unix-utils project. This is a \"stitch\" task in a code generation pipeline. The utility must print the system hostname to stdout with a trailing newline, support `--help` and `--version` flags, reject extra operands and unknown flags with error messages to stderr (exit 1), and call `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` at startup. The task specifies creating exactly one file: `cmd/hostname/main.go`. After implementation, it must pass `go build` and `go vet`.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Go Unix utility reimplementation verified via differential testing against GNU reference binaries\n   - SIGPIPE handler installation via `pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` — required for all cmd/ utilities\n   - Copyright header required: `// Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.` + `// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT`\n   - No git commands allowed — orchestrator manages git externally\n   - Function size limit: 40 lines max\n   - File size limit: 500 lines max\n   - Write all files before building/testing (no incremental compile-fix loops)\n   - Module path: `github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils`\n   - Build command: `go build -o bin/hostname ./cmd/hostname/`\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `docs/specs/software-requirements/srd047-hostname.yaml` (READ)\n     - Full SRD for the hostname utility\n     - R1.1: Print hostname + newline, exit 0\n     - R1.2: Output must match gethostname(2)\n     - R2.1: Extra operands → stderr error, exit 1\n     - R2.2: Unknown flags → stderr error, exit 1\n     - R3.1-R3.3: Differential testing requirements (not in scope for this task's file list)\n     - Non-g