0)\n   - Test that `bin/hostname --version` works (exit 0)\n\n8. Current Work:\n   I had just finished reading the SRD file (`docs/specs/software-requirements/srd047-hostname.yaml`) and was about to write the implementation file `cmd/hostname/main.go`. No code has been written yet. The task requirements from the SRD are clear and simple.\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Create `cmd/hostname/main.go` following the requirements. The implementation should:\n   - Start with the SPDX copyright header\n   - Import `fmt`, `os`, and `github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys`\n   - Call `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` at the start of main\n   - Parse args manually (since this is a minimal utility — no cobra needed for such a simple tool)\n   - Handle `--help` and `--version` flags\n   - Reject extra operands and unknown flags with error to stderr, exit 1\n   - Call `os.Hostname()` and print the result with `fmt.Println()`\n   - Then run `go build -o bin/hostname ./cmd/hostname/` and `go vet ./cmd/hostname/` to verify\n\n   Direct quote from task: \"files: - path: cmd/hostname/main.go action: create note: hostname utility -- prints the system hostname\"\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /Users/pdiddy/.claude/projects/-private-var-folders-dl-cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn-T-go-unix-utils-worktrees-5187/e074febc-29ca-4ae0-8d17-a11ea6e11daa.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e074febc-29ca-4ae0-8d17-a11ea6e11daa","uuid":"1d13f7cb-9b98-472f-ab57-960eb6528b38","timestamp":"2026-05-14T17:01:34.767Z","isSynthetic":true}
