{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011MRaKrfcy5ks6LWG9BTcpb","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t// Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.\n2\t// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n3\t\n4\t// Implements srd048-hostid R1.1-R1.2, R2.1-R2.2.\n5\tpackage main\n6\t\n7\timport (\n8\t\t\"fmt\"\n9\t\t\"os\"\n10\t\t\"strings\"\n11\t\t\"syscall\"\n12\t\n13\t\t\"github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys\"\n14\t)\n15\t\n16\tconst helpText = `Usage: hostid [OPTION]\n17\tPrint the numeric identifier (as a hexadecimal number) for the current host.\n18\t\n19\t      --help     display this help and exit\n20\t      --version  output version information and exit\n21\t`\n22\t\n23\tconst versionText = `hostid (go-unix-utils) dev\n24\t`\n25\t\n26\tfunc main() {\n27\t\tsys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()\n28\t\n29\t\targs := os.Args[1:]\n30\t\n31\t\tfor len(args) > 0 {\n32\t\t\tswitch args[0] {\n33\t\t\tcase \"--help\":\n34\t\t\t\tfmt.Fprint(os.Stdout, helpText)\n35\t\t\t\tos.Exit(0)\n36\t\t\tcase \"--version\":\n37\t\t\t\tfmt.Fprint(os.Stdout, versionText)\n38\t\t\t\tos.Exit(0)\n39\t\t\tcase \"--\":\n40\t\t\t\targs = args[1:]\n41\t\t\t\tgoto done\n42\t\t\tdefault:\n43\t\t\t\tif strings.HasPrefix(args[0], \"-\") && len(args[0]) > 1 {\n44\t\t\t\t\tfmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"hostid: unrecognized option '%s'\\n\", args[0])\n45\t\t\t\t\tfmt.Fprintln(os.Stderr, \"Try 'hostid --help' for more information.\")\n46\t\t\t\t\tos.Exit(1)\n47\t\t\t\t}\n48\t\t\t\tgoto done\n49\t\t\t}\n50\t\t}\n51\tdone:\n52\t\n53\t\tif len(args) > 0 {\n54\t\t\tfmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"hostid: extra operand '%s'\\n\", args[0])\n55\t\t\tfmt.Fprintln(os.Stderr, \"Try 'hostid --help' for more information.\")\n56\t\t\tos.Exit(1)\n57\t\t}\n58\t\n59\t\thostid, err := syscall.SysctlUint32(\"kern.hostid\")\n60\t\tif err != nil {\n61\t\t\tfmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"hostid: %v\\n\", err)\n62\t\t\tos.Exit(1)\n63\t\t}\n64\t\n65\t\tif _, err := fmt.Fprintf(os.Stdout, \"%08x\\n\", hostid); err != nil {\n66\t\t\tos.Exit(1)\n67\t\t}\n68\t}\n69\t\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_019FvJcRTDxcta8xJ4kZ4Ny5","session_id":"e074febc-29ca-4ae0-8d17-a11ea6e11daa","uuid":"5aee75ad-272a-4597-b277-b6ff19409cea","timestamp":"2026-05-14T17:01:51.534Z"}
