{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019FvJcRTDxcta8xJ4kZ4Ny5","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! I now have all the information you need. Let me provide a comprehensive report:\n\n## Report: Pattern Analysis from cmd/hostid/main.go\n\nI found **cmd/hostid/main.go** as an excellent reference for a simple utility. Here's the complete file with analysis of the patterns:\n\n### Full Contents of cmd/hostid/main.go:\n\n```go\n// Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n\n// Implements srd048-hostid R1.1-R1.2, R2.1-R2.2.\npackage main\n\nimport (\n\t\"fmt\"\n\t\"os\"\n\t\"strings\"\n\t\"syscall\"\n\n\t\"github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys\"\n)\n\nconst helpText = `Usage: hostid [OPTION]\nPrint the numeric identifier (as a hexadecimal number) for the current host.\n\n      --help     display this help and exit\n      --version  output version information and exit\n`\n\nconst versionText = `hostid (go-unix-utils) dev\n`\n\nfunc main() {\n\tsys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()\n\n\targs := os.Args[1:]\n\n\tfor len(args) > 0 {\n\t\tswitch args[0] {\n\t\tcase \"--help\":\n\t\t\tfmt.Fprint(os.Stdout, helpText)\n\t\t\tos.Exit(0)\n\t\tcase \"--version\":\n\t\t\tfmt.Fprint(os.Stdout, versionText)\n\t\t\tos.Exit(0)\n\t\tcase \"--\":\n\t\t\targs = args[1:]\n\t\t\tgoto done\n\t\tdefault:\n\t\t\tif strings.HasPrefix(args[0], \"-\") && len(args[0]) > 1 {\n\t\t\t\tfmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"hostid: unrecognized option '%s'\\n\", args[0])\n\t\t\t\tfmt.Fprintln(os.Stderr, \"Try 'hostid --help' for more information.\")\n\t\t\t\tos.Exit(1)\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\tgoto done\n\t\t}\n\t}\ndone:\n\n\tif len(args) > 0 {\n\t\tfmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"hostid: extra operand '%s'\\n\", args[0])\n\t\tfmt.Fprintln(os.Stderr, \"Try 'hostid --help' for more information.\")\n\t\tos.Exit(1)\n\t}\n\n\thostid, err := syscall.SysctlUint32(\"kern.hostid\")\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tfmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"hostid: %v\\n\", err)\n\t\tos.Exit(1)\n\t}\n\n\tif _, err := fmt.Fprintf(os.Stdout, \"%08x\\n\", hostid); err != nil {\n\t\tos.Exit(1)\n\t}\n}\n```\n\n### Pattern Details:\n\n1. **Copyright Header Format:**\n   - Line 1: `// Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.`\n   - Line 2: `// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT`\n   - Line 4: Implementation reference comment (e.g., `// Implements srd048-hostid R1.1-R1.2, R2.1-R2.2.`)\n\n2. **--help and --version Flag Handling:**\n   - Flags are checked in a manual loop using `switch` on `os.Args[1:]`\n   - `--help` prints `helpText` constant and exits with 0\n   - `--version` prints `versionText` constant and exits with 0\n   - `--` terminates option parsing (using `goto done`)\n\n3. **Error Message Format:**\n   - **Unknown flags:** `\"utility-name: unrecognized option 'flag'\\n\"` + hint line\n   - **Extra operands:** `\"utility-name: extra operand 'arg'\\n\"` + hint line\n   - **Hint format:** `\"Try 'utility-name --help' for more information.\\n\"`\n   - Errors are written to stderr using `fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, ...)`\n\n4. **SIGPIPE Handler Installation:**\n   - Called as the first line in `main()`: `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()`\n   - Implementation in `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5187/pkg/sys/sigpipe.go`\n   - Uses `signal.Notify` with a buffered channel and goroutine that exits with code 0 on SIGPIPE\n\n5. **Version Pattern:**\n   - Uses a `const versionText` (not a variable)\n   - Format: `\"program-name (go-unix-utils) dev\\n\"`\n   - This pattern is consistent across all utilities (hostid, arch, true, etc.)\n   - No external version constant/variable across utilities—each utility defines its own in the const block"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e074febc-29ca-4ae0-8d17-a11ea6e11daa","uuid":"d19b060d-ac3b-4899-9463-073acf722179","timestamp":"2026-05-14T17:02:09.167Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"In the repo at /private/var/fol